text:
Well, I've only got a couple of hours in so far. However, I'm confident that I have seen enough to make a review;
I love this game. It's beautiful, it plays well, and (for the most part) feels incredibly balanced. Dirty Bomb is a ♥♥♥♥in' blast. The artstyle in this game is pretty fun. It's bright and colorful but realistic enough the immerse you in a futuristic world. The controls are tight and responsive and it's comfortable. The movement is fun; you've got wall jumps and long jumps. Learning the maps and utilizing these techniques, which are simple and easy to master, can give you a huge advantage in movement against the enemy team. Speaking of movement, the tutorial basically crams the whole "keep moving" thing down your throat. And the tutorial is so right. If you put somebody who is firing from the hip against one who is nearly stationary and firing through sights the hip-shooter is going to win. As long as you can move faster than they can aim you can kill them. The balancing is fine; I mean, there isn't much to talk about until you've played it. But, overall, it seems fair. Of course, I've only really played Aura, Skyhammer, and Fletcher so I can't really tell you much other than "it's fine" and "it seems fair".
This game is like a glorious mixture of Battlefield, Team Fortress 2, and Overwatch. I'm in love, I think. I look forward to many more hours.

